Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 03:05:20 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] feat(plans): a no-candidate refusal names which rules broke
 which candidate

Red team arm 2: three hard constraints on file made plans/generate answer the generic
"No feasible plan candidates" whose details carried only counts, so the traveller could not tell
which assertion killed the plan. The per-candidate rejections the gate already produces are now
collected and put into the refusal's details, which main.py forwards verbatim - no main.py change,
no rewritten sentence, no new vocabulary.

Also fixes the false red my own two-hard node had: a candidate can conflict with both rules at the
same stop, and the product correctly names both, so the judge compares presence against the
expected structure instead of assuming at most one conflict per candidate.
